WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.450
Shindou...

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.770
Megalodon!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.990
It's <i>me</i>  who will protect the goal!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.410
Wild Dunk!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.380
He did it!

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:23.940
Ibuki!

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.080
Yes!

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.090
A hissatsu technique, huh...

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.100
Just watch! I can do it too!

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.120
If this keeps up, I...

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.360
I have to show results!

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.200
Sakura?

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.650
Football Frontier International Vision 2's Asia district prelims!

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:32.120
The match between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Australia's Big Waves is currently in its second half!

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.670
The score is 2-1 with Big Waves in the lead!

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.740
How will Inazuma Japan get through Big Waves' tight defense?

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.690
You can't take your eyes off this match!

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.310
<i>Check that out! Did you see that, Shindou?!</i>

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.500
<i>That's what the goalkeeper should be doing.</i>

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.150
He still won't accept me...

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.560
Good job, goalkeeper!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.700
Nice save!

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.910
Why do they keep complimenting him?

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:05.780
Shindou-san!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.050
Just look at everyone!

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:18.520
They look so much more focused after seeing Ibuki make his hissatsu technique, don't you think?

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.090
Yeah.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.220
But God's Baton no longer works for us.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.720
What would you do to break through this deadlock?

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.400
We should keep attacking!

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.980
If we pass the ball around between you, Tsurugi, me, and Matatagi...

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.560
That looks to be our only option.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.570
Guys! There's still time!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.140
Let's take back one point first!

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:43.990
Shindou!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.420
Nice pass, Ibuki!

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.120
Not nice enough.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.710
I'll stop you!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.770
Presto Turn V2!

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:01.960
Tenma!

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:02.690
Okay!

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:05.640
Sakura!

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:06.510
That girl!

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.820
I have to show results faster than the others.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:10.850
So...

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.350
I'm going to try my own hissatsu technique!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.400
Shindou makes a cut and stops the danger!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.770
Just what are you doing?!

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.530
What's she thinking, trying to use a hissatsu technique there?

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:33.060
I really wish she would stop messing up our rhythm.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.490
Everyone, let's focus on the game!

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.430
It's just like that time...

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.800
Congratulations on second place.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.490
Thank you.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.570
Congratulations on winning.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.210
Thank you!

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.500
I don't want to go through that again...

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.410
<i>Soccer is supposed to be fun...</i>

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.970
<i>But you look miserable.</i>

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.840
<i>What are you talking about, Captain?</i>

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.730
<i>Do I look miserable to you right now?</i>

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.940
She <i>is</i>  feeling miserable.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.440
Why...

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.300
Why won't it work?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.670
Don't rush!

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.500
Take a deep breath, Sakura!

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.080
What's the matter with Sakura-san?

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.010
She seems really impatient about something.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.330
Coach! Do you really intend to let this go on?

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.650
I can't show myself looking like a fool to them any longer.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.700
In that case...

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:31.700
Konoha!

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:37.200
Sakura?!

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.920
Nozaki and Morimura have crashed into each other!

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.300
Oh, come on! Did you see that?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.660
She definitely ran into her on purpose.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:55.890
She's pushing around the Inazuma Japan team, it's so sad.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:01.100
Are you okay?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.330
Well, that's strange.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.320
You couldn't have hurt your leg from that angle.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:08.980
Um...

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.130
It was my fault.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.010
I've been feeling dizzy today, and I'm not sure why.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:21.210
I see.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:24.460
So that's why you weren't doing as great as you did during practice.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:30.090
I'm really sorry for being a bother to everyone.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.640
We don't have reserve players to switch with her.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.300
We'll have to switch her position around.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.100
Yeah.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.580
I knew we should have included reserve players.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.040
We should have stopped her from this soccer nonsense.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.320
Yes.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.280
Papa... Mama...

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.660
What went wrong in your performance today?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.330
I know you could've done better than her.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.250
Let's not hang up this medal.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.320
Have you got that, Sakura?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:14.700
If we hang this up, it means that we admit that there is someone out there who is better than you.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:19.020
Yes. You deserve to be shining at the very top.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.900
After all, you are our daughter.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.800
You aren't the type of athlete to fail at a place like this.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.600
I know you can do more.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.610
Concentrate on what you must do.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.370
Okay! I'll try even harder!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.470
I'm sorry for not showing the results you want...

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.320
Papa... Mama...

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.840
Hey, Sakura.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.670
W-What, Captain?

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:57.390
Was it fun when you were performing for rhythmic gymnastics?

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.200
Huh?

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.840
Of course!

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.390
It was very fun.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.840
Then I want you to remember how you felt that time.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:09.480
I have this feeling that you aren't enjoying soccer from the heart right now.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.770
Enjoying soccer?

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:13.000
Tenma!

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.480
We're going into position!

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:16.500
O-Okay!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.240
Let's try our very best right now on what we're able to do!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.370
Okay, Sakura?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.250
Inazuma Japan changes position for Nozaki and Tetsukado.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.290
We're counting on you, Tetsukado!

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:34.460
Leave it to me!

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.850
What does he mean, I'm not enjoying soccer?

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:40.270
Results are everything in sports.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:44.100
There's nothing fun about it if I'm not number one!

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:46.980
Matatagi!

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.890
They've lost one functioning person!

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.270
Make an all-out attack!

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.320
We'll subdue them with an overwhelming victory!

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:54.440
Yes, sir!

00:09:58.730 --> 00:09:59.490
This again!

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:00.950
Suck Out!

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:09.790
Matatagi is stopped by Suck Out yet again!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.880
We cannot afford to lose!

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.260
Everyone but the goalkeeper, move up!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:16.470
Okay!

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.500
Big Waves continues to attack!

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.510
Inazuma Japan is stuck defending!

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.350
It's taking everything we can just to hold out against them...

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.350
Just what can we do?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:32.230
Oh no!

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:36.440
Aw, we're going to lose a point.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.950
Well, it's not a match I got to shine in, so it doesn't matter.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.280
It's mine!

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:46.940
I'll stop it!

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.780
Ibuki stops the ball!

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:52.620
What?!

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:53.750
He stopped it!

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.600
That guy...

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.080
Nice clear, Ibuki!

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.010
Make the goal, Octa!

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.520
Megalodon!

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:15.760
If I lose here, it's all over...

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.940
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:26.040
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.370
Megalodon!

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.650
If I lose here, it's all over...

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.370
I won't let it end like this!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.890
Wild Dunk!

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:51.160
Ibuki!

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:54.070
He stops it!

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:57.400
Goalkeeper Ibuki magnificently saves the team!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:58.970
All right!

00:11:58.970 --> 00:11:59.860
Nice job, goalkeeper!

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:01.800
Hey, not bad!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.110
Ibuki, that was so cool...

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.890
I think I've got a grasp on the timing.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.020
Don't just stand there!

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.080
Attack quickly!

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:21.260
Nozaki!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.800
Okay!

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:23.290
Over here!

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.260
Will this become Inazuma Japan's counterattack?

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.060
Where are you aiming?

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.310
Amazing! Matatagi catches up to it!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.060
What?!

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.890
I won't lose either!

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:39.110
Matatagi?

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.660
Parkour Attack!

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.800
Goal!

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:56.490
Matatagi's shoot finally brings Inazuma Japan to a tie!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:59.570
I made it in... with a hissatsu technique...

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:00.750
I made it in!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.570
You go, Hayato-niichan!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.470
So cool!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:06.220
He actually succeeded with a hissatsu technique...

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:07.720
Matatagi!

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.450
That shoot was incredible!

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.400
You're not bad stuff!

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.730
Scoring the goal in that way, yeah.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.700
Both your angle and speed were perfect.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.860
Pretty good moves.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:21.190
It was slightly higher than I anticipated.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.440
<i>If I lose here, it's all over...</i>

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.280
<i>I won't let it end like this!</i>

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.930
It would all be over, huh...

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.040
Sakura!

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.120
You made a nice assist there, Sakura!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.130
Huh? I didn't do anything...

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:44.010
But without your pass, we wouldn't have had the chance to make that goal!

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.510
My pass?

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:47.680
That's right.

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.400
Soccer is teamwork.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:51.860
So I want you to be happy about this with us!

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.290
This point was made through both you and the others!

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:01.860
I still have to show them that I'm good at this.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.020
Um, hey, Captain?

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:06.320
My leg feels better.

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.220
Really?

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.320
Are you sure you're okay?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.410
I'm fine. I'll do my best!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.450
Now, the match resumes!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:18.460
Both teams are tied. Which of them will achieve victory?!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.200
I can do this too!

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.000
Close one, Tetsukado!

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:27.820
S-Sure.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.280
You'll get it next time!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.180
I'll have it perfectly calculated next time.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.230
They've begun to encourage each other.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:40.940
While it is minor, it is still a big change.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:44.190
Octa!

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.940
An opportunity has arisen for Inazuma Japan!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:49.320
Sakura!

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.000
I have to be the best!

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.000
The best?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.800
Hissatsu tactics!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:06.590
Suck Out!

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:07.670
Yeah!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.480
How can I get through this?

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.940
Shindou-san! Your God's Baton!

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:26.150
What are you thinking? There's no way it can work...

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.200
It has to be higher than before!

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.690
I'll definitely get above it!

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:31.490
Sakura...

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.210
Shindou-san, please!

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.370
God's Baton!

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.670
I can do it!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.420
The fearsome Suck Out stops them in their tracks once again!

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:50.720
Sakura!

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.650
I failed again...

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.970
You barely made it with your timing.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.100
If you hadn't tried to jump higher than what I had directed, you would have been able to pull it off.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:08.800
You almost had it!

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:10.240
Almost had it?

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.740
Just a little more and you definitely would have succeeded!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.550
What are you talking about?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.300
I failed!

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.240
Hey, I always fail!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.860
It's because we fail that it feels great when we succeed!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.380
It's because we fail that it feels great when we succeed...

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.340
C'mon, the match isn't over yet.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.420
Let's do our best, Sakura.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:33.930
That's just like Tenma.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.480
Just a few minutes remain!

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:38.260
Will the match be decided with this single play?!

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:44.390
Nozaki-san!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.150
Suck Out!

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.070
Shindou-san!

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:57.330
She can do it! Sakura will definitely succeed!

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:58.030
Okay.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.870
God's Baton: Fire Illusion!

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:12.510
Will she be able to keep up with that?

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:17.760
I am not... scared of failing!

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.300
Please!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.730
I did it!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:28.950
Good job, Sakura!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:30.570
Good!

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.190
Show them what you can do!

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.190
Sakura!

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.880
I can make the goal!

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:36.860
I won't let you pass!

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.950
<i>I want you to be happy about this with us!</i>

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:48.210
<i>This point was made through both you and the others!</i>

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.130
The angle of incidence and velocity are both perfect!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.100
If I kick the ball in by matching the timing...!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:07.220
Huh...?

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:08.560
It went in...

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.730
Goal!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.420
Manabe makes the goal!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:16.570
His shoot takes the goalkeeper by surprise and scores an additional point for the team!

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:19.370
That was amazing, Manabe!

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.050
Nice shoot!

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:23.620
I-It was all part of my calculations.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:25.580
You too, Sakura! That was a nice pass!

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:27.440
Captain...

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:28.540
Yeah.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.350
Why didn't she make the shoot herself?

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.080
Sakura.

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.760
Is there someone you know sitting in the stands?

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:40.890
Yeah...

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.580
My Papa and Mama.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:47.980
But since I didn't get to do much, I don't think they're happy with me at all.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.120
That's not true.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.980
Without your pass, we wouldn't have made the goal.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.610
Tsurugi-kun...

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.180
When they see you enjoying yourself, they'll understand.

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:03.610
Okay!

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.090
Inazuma Japan rides on their momentum!

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:09.410
Will they be able to keep this up to the end?!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.500
Sakura...

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.380
Thank goodness.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.840
This match isn't worth watching.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.010
But...

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.620
I've never seen her smile like that so much before.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:29.140
The match is over!

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:33.140
Inazuma Japan makes a turnabout victory with a score of 3-2!

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.650
All right!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.740
Damn it...

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.320
No...

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.200
We... lost...

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:55.800
Are you telling me that this team is actually incredibly powerful?

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:15.230
<i>I have to be the best!</i>

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:18.500
Sakura!

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:19.690
What?

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.970
Um, well, I think that...

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.700
Being number one with everyone is fine in its own way, isn't it?

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.620
Of course it is, Captain!

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.000
Sakura.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:34.540
Tenma!

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:35.380
Here!

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:44.050
Be number one with everyone, huh?

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.600
I guess that works too.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:53.250
Your team is gradually beginning to show their abilities.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:54.100
Yes.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:59.370
But the opponent that Inazuma Japan will face now is nothing like that.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:05.770
Their fighting style now won't even count as a warming up session for these opponents.

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:08.160
You are aware of this as well.

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:15.420
I will tell you, the power that they've so far displayed is only a warm up itself.

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:21.380
As always, I do wonder where that baseless confidence of yours comes from...

00:22:52.850 --> 00:23:07.860
Next Episode

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:56.100
There's another problem?!

00:22:56.210 --> 00:22:57.520
This time, it's Kusaka?!

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:01.770
His smiling face and demonic face bring a storm upon Inazuma Japan!

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:04.230
Next, Kusaka's Two Faces!

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:06.080
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:07.860
<b>Kusaka's Two Faces</b>

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:19.100
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:25.900
It's because we fail that it feels great when we succeed!

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:26.610
That's all!
